@startuml time_sync_timing
title NTP four-timestamp Time Synchronization — generating T1..T4 (BC <-> RT, sub-address 1, SystemHandler)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30

' Two clocks on a shared wall-clock axis (ms, illustrative values).
' T1/T4 are read off the BC clock; T2/T3 off the RT clock. The standing gap
' between the two clocks IS the offset the exchange solves for.
' (note top/bottom of <player> is unsupported in this PlantUML; the four
'  timestamps are marked on the waveform states and defined in the legend.)
robust "Bus Controller\n(BC clock)" as BC
robust "Remote Terminal\n(RT clock)" as RT

@0
BC is Idle
RT is Idle

@10
BC is "T1: TX probe"

@30
RT is "T2: RX probe"

@45
RT is "T3: TX reply"

@65
BC is "T4: RX reply"
RT is Idle

@80
BC is Idle

' --- connecting lines: the two propagation legs that carry the timestamps ---
BC@10 -> RT@30 : SYNC_PROBE [T1] : T1 send -> T2 recv
RT@45 -> BC@65 : reply [T2,T3] : T3 send -> T4 recv

' --- intervals the four timestamps define ---
highlight 30 to 45 #WhiteSmoke : RT handling (T3 - T2)
@10 <-> @65 : round trip = T4 - T1

legend bottom
  Four timestamps captured per exchange (clock.now_ms()):
    T1 = BC clock when SYNC_PROBE is sent
    T2 = RT clock when the probe arrives
    T3 = RT clock just before the [T2,T3] reply is sent  (T3 - T2 = RT handling time)
    T4 = BC clock when that reply arrives back at the BC
  From them the RT computes (compute_sync_fixed, sync.cpp):
    path_delay = ((T4 - T1) - (T3 - T2)) / 2     (one-way, RTT/2)
    offset     = ((T1 - T2) + (T4 - T3)) / 2     (BC - RT; + when BC leads)
  Removing (T3 - T2) takes the RT's own handling time out of the round trip.
  T4 is delivered to the RT afterward in the SYNC_FINAL command (opcode 0x07).
endlegend

@enduml
